cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use KINO, please cite it as below."
title: "KINO: KInematic lensing iNference and mock-Observations"
abstract: >-
  A Python toolkit to simulate and test the inference of kinematic lensing
  (KL) -- the measurement of weak gravitational shear from the distorted
  velocity field of an individual disc galaxy -- across both integral-field
  unit (IFU) and slit/grism spectrograph observing modes.
authors:
  - family-names: "Zamorano Vitorelli"
    given-names: "Andre"
    email: "andrezvitorelli@gmail.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/andrevitorelli/KINO"
license: MIT
